  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">West Africa Sub-Regional Network For Results-Based Education Sector Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aim to improve the quality of education in Francophone West Africa by establishing a network of which generate the knowledge base, policy tools and expertise networks necessary to systematically address education issues in 8 countries of the sub-region. Its overall development objective is to help strengthen the capacity the capacity of sub-regional institutions that are responsible for measuring student learning outcomes and to ensure that findings from the assessments are used to improve teaching and learning. Under three broad categories of technical assistance, training and goods the IDF funds would specifically be used to (i) create a regional network supported by an established body, CONFEMEN; (ii) develop the capacity of policy makers and analysts for measuring learning and understanding the impact of policy decisions on results; and (iii) to provide of goods and equipment to support project the project&apos;s activities.</narrative>
  </description>
